  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the skewness, i.e., whether more probability is assigned to favorable (here, less negative or zero) outcomes. The relevant information—probabilities of losses and their magnitudes—is available, but the individual does not use it in a way that reflects skewness assessment. Instead, the individual focuses only on the size of the loss, favoring the smaller loss amount. The reason would prefer Lottery B (less probability on loss, more left-skewed), but the individual chooses A for a different rationale. There is no indication that the person considered the relative concentration of probability mass on favorable outcomes. The justification is based on loss magnitude, not distributional shape. Therefore, the decision reason based on skewness was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
